  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual metaphor implying personal criminality",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'when you've finished with your life of crime', which uses the deictic 'your' to directly address the viewer, implying that the viewer is the one who has 'finished' a 'life of crime'. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user is metaphorically mapped onto the criminalized identity described in the text, even though the visual material (the surgeon) is not directly addressed. The projection is onto the textual material, which frames the user as the subject of the metaphorical statement.",
